{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command '$p='\"'docs/test/test-cases.toml';\"'$s=Get-Content -Raw $p;foreach($id in '\"'333','410','411','412'){[regex]::Match(\"'$s,\"(?ms)''^'\"\\\\[test\\\\.TC-\"'$id'\"\\\\].*?(?=\"'^'\"\\\\[test\\\\.|\\\\z)\\\").Value}; \"'$p='\"'docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml';\"'$s=Get-Content -Raw $p;[regex]::Match($s,'\"'(?ms)\"'^'\"\\\\[design\\\\.LLR-365\\\\].*?(?=\"'^'\"\\\\[design\\\\.LLR-|\\\\z)').Value\"","aggregated_output":"[test.TC-333]\nverifies = [\"SR-146\", \"SR-154\", \"SR-235\", \"LLR-313\", \"IF-046\", \"IF-047\", \"IF-288\", \"IF-289\"]\nlevel = \"Integration\"\nmethod = \"Run test_a_rendered_review_brief_carries_the_kit_clauses_and_the_lane_facts, test_a_narrow_round_names_the_findings_it_answers, test_a_narrow_round_without_findings_and_a_full_one_with_them_are_refused, test_a_named_input_that_is_not_there_refuses, test_an_unfilled_slot_refuses_and_no_brief_is_written, test_the_scope_critique_carries_ruling_twos_questions_and_its_rubric, test_a_filed_coordinator_review_appears_in_the_rollup, test_a_bracketed_word_that_is_not_a_severity_never_refuses_a_filing, test_a_malformed_review_is_refused_and_nothing_is_filed, test_a_round_with_no_tests_refuses, test_an_empty_or_missing_named_input_refuses, test_the_critique_render_refuses_a_missing_spec, test_the_command_line_refuses_a_lane_the_git_reads_reject, test_a_review_render_exits_zero_and_writes_only_the_brief, and test_filing_a_review_exits_zero_and_writes_only_the_round_file. Render full and narrow review briefs and a scope critique over a temporary lane; refuse an empty test list, empty or missing named inputs, and a critique without a specification; on a real lane, drive detached, non-commit and non-ancestor command-line refusals, then successful review rendering and filing; file a well-formed review and malformed review cases, including a non-severity bracketed bullet beside a matching declared finding count, and attempt filing for a lane whose branch the round reader cannot read back as a review scope, before rendering the rollup. Per commit, render the first and revised single-plan briefs and exercise their missing-input and unfilled-slot refusals. Only in the full suite, exercise plan-critique rendering, filing, the pass form and their refusals, including a MINOR before a MAJOR with dismissal of F2, two blocking findings with only one dismissed, a revision that misses a first finding, and a committed critique whose working copy differs only by line-ending conversion or has a real uncommitted edit. Render the scope critique with every registry present and with one absent; render ordinary, absent-stance, and convergence review briefs in process and at the command line; prove their distinct reading scopes; refuse narrow convergence and unknown stance; file a convergence-tagged finding; check the live scope rubric against the rendered registry set and the plan-critique every-class and confirming-round reachability gates; pin single-plan registry lines; and, in the full suite, prove that SUCCESSOR never writes a plan-cap pass record.\"\ntier = \"Full\"\nexpected = \"A complete attended review or critique brief has no unfilled slot and carries the shipped review clauses, lane facts or scope rubric as applicable. An empty test list, invalid round shape, missing specification, unreadable or empty named input, unfilled template slot, malformed or unbound verdict (without exactly one line whose keyword, compared case-insensitively, is VERDICT in the canonical form `VERDICT: <APPROVE|CHANGES-REQUESTED> findings=<digits>`), and a lane branch the round reader cannot read as a review scope are refused without a requested file or review record. A bracketed non-severity bullet beside N declared-severity findings and findings=N is filed, and its rollup shows N. A detached lane, non-commit revision or non-ancestor base returns exit 2 with no output file and a clean repository. A successful review returns exit 0 and writes only its brief with full resolved revisions and the reviewed tip; successful filing returns exit 0 and adds only the next review-round record. A valid filed review is rendered in the lane review history. Per-commit brief renders and their stated refusals remain in the smoke tier. The full suite proves that the first critique covers Done-when alone, the second also covers first-critique finding identifiers without their text, a revision missing a first finding is refused at render, a MINOR before a MAJOR passes on dismissal of F2, two blocking findings with only one dismissed are refused, and a committed critique changed only by line-ending conversion passes while a real uncommitted edit is refused. The second plan critique's brief never carries the first critique's verdict or any finding's text. A successfully filed critique writes only its record. A plan critique with a missing rubric, plan or specification, or a beyond delta, refuses without output. The shipped planner template is in the catalogue. The scope critique names the five declared registries and marks only an absent one; absent stance and ordinary output match and contain no stance line; convergence has one fixed line after the range; narrow convergence refuses without a brief; a tagged finding files as one finding; and SUCCESSOR at the plan cap writes no pass record. An ordinary review reading scope includes the delegated-decisions record and filed plan critiques, while a convergence scope excludes both. A plan critique ties every severity class to reachability, counts a fail-open, data-loss, or security path only when a supported workflow or the kit's own routes reach it, and limits a rare or contrived path to MINOR at most or dismissal; its confirming round treats a new finding as BLOCKER or MAJOR only when it is a reachable fail-open, data-loss, or Done-when gap.\"\nautomated = \"Yes\"\nevidence = \"te